# Hosted GitHub sign-in application

Register a separate OAuth App or GitHub App user authorization-code flow.
After infrastructure deployment, use the actual dashboardHostName output:

- Homepage: `https://DASHBOARD_HOST/`
- Authorization callback: `https://DASHBOARD_HOST/auth/callback`
- Client ID: the reviewed githubClientId parameter.
- Client secret: the githubClientSecret Key Vault reference, NOT a literal.

Do not repoint an existing deployment's callback. GitHub Apps using
organization/team authorization need Members: read and an approved installation
in each allowed organization; classic OAuth Apps need approved organization
access where third-party restrictions apply. Enable expiring user tokens for
GitHub Apps. Test allowed AND disallowed identities.

Actions snapshot acquisition needs no new collection App in these compact
profiles. Collection, session lake, gateway, hosted CLI and broker execution
are not enabled. Existing control-repository App credentials and safe outputs
retain their separate reviewed policy; topology generation grants no reach.
